Element Selector in CSS
------------------------
1) An element selector (also called a type selector) targets HTML elements 
   by their tag name.

2) It applies styles to ALL elements of that type on the page.

3) Example:
   
   p {
       color: red;
   }

   This will make all <p> elements red.

4) Common element selectors:
   - p
   - h1, h2, h3
   - div
   - span
   - img
   - a

5) Element selectors are useful for general styling, but avoid overusing them
   when you need more specific control — use classes or IDs instead.

